ARCHITECTURE (mirrors the A7 StatisticsPage / DrivetrainHealthPage precedents)
  SafetySettingsPageModel.kt      framework-free: registration ids (safetySettings / /safety-settings / SLUG);
                                  SafetySnapshot + SecurityLatest + SafetyFeature decode; the safety-enum
                                  normalization choke point (cleanSafetyEnum / isSafetyEnumActive — web
                                  lib/safetyEnum.ts, incl. the SpeedAssistLevelNone⇒Off + AEB inverted cases);
                                  the 0..9 score + the nine feature cards; toSafetyChartData (ascending step
                                  series) + sortedSafetyHistory (newest-first); SafetyDisplayPrefs (web useUnits —
                                  SI metres → display distance via the shared convertDistanceFromSI); Resource.mapData;
                                  recordSafetySettingsOpened (PII-safe view.opened).
  SafetySettingsPageSource.kt     seam over a page-local SafetyExtrasRepository (CachingRepository<JsonElement>,
                                  CacheDomain.VehicleSystems) for the three reads the shared stores have no method
                                  for — /security/latest (web useSecurityLatest), /safety/latest (web useQuery) and
                                  /safety?limit=100 (web useQuery) — plus SettingsStore.settings (web useUnits) +
                                  SelectedVehicleStore (web useSelectedVehicle). Same resilient client + offline
                                  cache as every other feed; the StatisticsExtrasRepository precedent.
  SafetySettingsPageViewModel.kt  BaseFeedViewModel; state: StateFlow<UiState<SafetySnapshot>> (primary, isEmpty=!hasData),
                                  history: StateFlow<UiState<List<SafetySnapshot>>>, security: StateFlow<SecurityLatest>
                                  (the panel always renders, em dash on missing), displayPrefs: StateFlow<SafetyDisplayPrefs>;
                                  scoped to the active vehicle, refresh()/retry()/recordViewOpened().
  SafetySettingsPage.kt           stateless Compose render layer — chrome (title/subtitle/freshness/VehicleSelect) +
                                  the loading/error/empty/loaded body; every panel drawn from the decoded models.
  SafetySettingsPageIcons.kt      web lucide glyphs: Lock/Shield re-exported from the shared catalogs; UserCheck/
                                  Armchair/Navigation/Cpu/AlertCircle authored as 24×24 stroked vectors.
  SafetySettingsPageHost.kt       binds the source for the `safetySettings` route via safetySettingsPageSourceOf;
                                  registered once at process start (TeslaSyncApplication L333).

  Manifest-declared data source = useSecurityLatest only; the page ALSO reads /safety/latest + /safety (bare web
  useQuery, not named hooks, so the generator missed them). All three are implemented — the score / feature cards /
  driving-stats panels and the chart + history table cannot render at parity without them (no scope narrowing).

