STRING CATALOG
  31 of the 59 keys already existed in res/values/strings.xml (translation_safety_*, translation_On/Off/Enabled/
  Disabled/AEB/BSC/…/error_loadFailed/enabled — generated from the shared i18n catalog with the verbatim web
  default values). The remaining 28 (the literal-as-key ADAS labels/descriptions, the section titles, the three
  empty/error messages) were absent from the web i18n source, so they were added to res/values/strings.xml (an
  allowed file) with the verbatim web default text and the canonical generator key transform
  ("translation." + key, every non-[A-Za-z0-9_] char → '_'; e.g. "ADAS features, safety score, and driving stats"
  → translation_ADAS_features__safety_score__and_driving_stats, "No history records found." →
  translation_No_history_records_found_). The default values/ catalog is the only string source touched: the build
  runs no i18n generation, and MissingTranslation/ExtraTranslation are disabled (app/build.gradle.kts L114) because
  ar/he ship as full English fallback, so the ar/he mirrors are not required. The "%" percent unit (gauge + score
  card) is the web's own non-internationalized literal.

A11Y / THEME / UNITS (ADR-015)
  - Each live SignalCard carries a merged TalkBack content description ("<label>: <value>") via clearAndSetSemantics
    (L378); the RadialGauge exposes one screen-reader description (A3 component); the safety-states ChartContainer
    exposes the accessible data-table fallback ([Time, AEB, BSCW, ELDA] rows, L517-520) for the opaque canvas.
  - Colours/typography come from MaterialTheme + the per-theme TeslaTokens.status palette (P1/S9); dark + dynamic
    colour honoured. The score gauge/badge colour is the web scoreColor (≥80 success / ≥50 warning / else danger),
    a dynamic value, not a static literal — the DarkStatusColors hexes (#10B981/#F59E0B/#EF4444) are the SAME the
    web scoreColor uses. Touch targets use the shared component sizing.
  - SI metres (the misnamed *_miles_since_reset fields — content is metres) are converted only at the display
    boundary (SafetyDisplayPrefs.distance → shared convertDistanceFromSI); the page is Compose-native — the line
    chart uses the A3 LineChartWrapper (no webview). The web page has no map (0 maps).

